  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the graph of \\(y = mx + b\\), where \\(m\\) and \\(b\\) are constants, passes through the points \\((3, 0)\\) and \\((0, -6)\\). What is the value of \\(m + b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The point \\((0, -6)\\) gives \\(b = -6\\).",
    "Slope: \\(m = \\frac{0 - (-6)}{3 - 0} = 2\\).",
    "\\(m + b = 2 + (-6) = -4\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "m, b = symbols('m b')\nsol = solve([Eq(3*m + b, 0), Eq(b, -6)], [m, b])\nans = sol[m] + sol[b]\nassert ans == -4\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == ans and len(spr_answers) == 1",
